  "graph": {
    "nodes": [
      {
        "id": "1",
        "kind": "comment",
        "config": {
          "text": "Study: a sampler and drum machine (pads from MIDI, the computer keys, and the mouse; velocity layers; round robin; choke; slices of a loop; a keymapped instrument; resampling), built from today's nodes.\n\nA Pads grid plays everything: notes 36 to 43 are eight slices of one drum loop, cut at its hits by a Slicer; 44 is a snare with a soft and a hard layer and two round-robin samples; 45 and 46 are a closed and an open hat, the closed one choking the open one; 47 plays what the Resample section recorded. Each pad lights when its note plays and plays as hard as it's hit. The Keys section is a two-zone sampled instrument inside a Voices node.\n\nWhat a sampler has that this can't: a pad block that carries its own sample and a library of kits. Read docs/GAPS.md."
        },
        "ui": {
          "pos": [
            0.0,
            -700.0
          ],
          "size": [
            760.0,
            300.0
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "7",
        "kind": "comment",
        "config": {
          "text": "Players: a MIDI keyboard, the computer keys (Z S X D C V G B are notes 36 to 43 with Play keys on), the Pads grid, and a demo MIDI Pattern that plays the kit in a render, merged into one MIDI stream that also lights the pads."
        },
        "ui": {
          "pos": [
            0.0,
            -320.0
          ],
          "size": [
            560.0,
            96.0
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "c0",
        "kind": "comment",
        "config": {
          "text": "Slices: a Sample of the drum loop into a Slicer that cuts it at its hits. Notes from 36 play the slices in order, at the note's velocity; the Slicer's Node tab shows where it cut."
        },
        "ui": {
          "pos": [
            660.0,
            -320.0
          ],
          "size": [
            560.0,
            96.0
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "21",
        "kind": "comment",
        "config": {
          "text": "Velocity layers and round robin: Note Split gives the snare's note a trigger and a velocity, Zones splits it into a soft and a hard layer by velocity, and a Counter steps two Routes so each layer alternates between two samples. The hats share a choke group, so the closed one ends the open one."
        },
        "ui": {
          "pos": [
            990.0,
            300.0
          ],
          "size": [
            620.0,
            110.0
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "4a",
        "kind": "comment",
        "config": {
          "text": "The Keys body: a Voice feeds Zones (notes below C4, and C4 and up), whose triggers start one of two Samplers; an ADSR shapes the level. Drag the zones in the Zones node's Node tab to move the split."
        },
        "ui": {
          "pos": [
            0.0,
            1380.0
          ],
          "size": [
            600.0,
            110.0
          ]
        }
      },
